`dzil build` fails before it produces a tarball.

Two causes, both in the distribution metadata:
1. dist.ini has `[@Author::GETTY]` with `license = Perl_5` and a `copyright_holder`, but no `copyright_year`.
2. There is no committed LICENSE file in the repository root.

`[@Author::GETTY]` checks the LICENSE against license, copyright_holder and copyright_year and aborts the build when the file is missing or no longer matches. Because `Git::GatherDir` only sees tracked files, a LICENSE that is generated but not `git add`ed is invisible to the build as well.

What to do:
1. Add `copyright_year = <the year the dist was first published>` to dist.ini — look up the year of the 0.001 release from the git log, not from today's date.
2. Run `dzil genlicense` to create the LICENSE file.
3. `git add LICENSE` — the add is mandatory, the build gathers through git.
4. Run `dzil build` and `dzil test` and make sure both finish cleanly.

Note for the release manager: the dist.ini `$VERSION` is 0.003, which is the next unreleased version after the 0.002 release. Never copy a version back from CPAN, and never bump it in this card — a version bump is not part of the work.

Do not run `dzil release`, do not tag, do not push.

